{"requirements":[{"id":"restore_helpdesk","requirement":"Restore tickets.sql into a PostgreSQL database named helpdesk while preserving the imported ticket IDs and text.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The helpdesk database was created, the supplied export restored successfully, and direct final queries showed exactly the imported rows: 1/Printer queue, 2/Scanner cable, and 100/Office move. The same data remained after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5cff1f1cb6c54040","cmd-efd60755ab664e7f","cmd-eb87766b955d42b7","cmd-c07353c020164623","cmd-64376be8ba834f04"]},{"id":"repair_id_allocation","requirement":"Repair automatic ID allocation so inserts without an explicit ID receive unique IDs greater than the imported maximum.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initially stale sequence was observed, then set to the imported maximum of 100. Transactional implicit-insert tests returned ID 101 both before and after restart. Each test row was rolled back and the sequence restored to the correct final state of 100 with is_called=true.","evidence_ids":["cmd-84d4f932ad194860","cmd-a2a5a04fa3954178","cmd-eb87766b955d42b7","cmd-64376be8ba834f04"]},{"id":"preserve_source_export","requirement":"Preserve the source export under /srv/legacy2/postgresql-sequence-repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"tickets.sql remained at the required path with its baseline size and SHA-256 hash unchanged, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-0c1e1291f799439c","cmd-eb87766b955d42b7","cmd-c07353c020164623","cmd-64376be8ba834f04"]},{"id":"preserve_legacy_platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were unchanged through the work and restart. PostgreSQL 8.2.11 was installed from the Ubuntu 7.10 archive and was directly observed online.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0c1e1291f799439c","cmd-9bab005779cf4793","cmd-b3bdb54fdd264aeb","cmd-1a85c597f5bf4938","cmd-c07353c020164623","cmd-64376be8ba834f04","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. apt-get update and the PostgreSQL installation established the necessary compatible prerequisite; database creation, import, and setval implemented the requested state; transactional inserts and compensating sequence resets were bounded final checks; and the reboot was required provider-wide restart evidence. The temporary reboot log did not remain after recovery. Package health remained clean, and no executor-caused temporary-file residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3f052ab7e99746dc","cmd-b3bdb54fdd264aeb","cmd-5cff1f1cb6c54040","cmd-efd60755ab664e7f","cmd-a2a5a04fa3954178","cmd-eb87766b955d42b7","cmd-6e54e876d99c462c","cmd-64376be8ba834f04","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were recorded, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed, and PostgreSQL, ticket data, sequence behavior, source export, OS, and kernel recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Systemd failed-service collection was unsupported on this legacy SysV platform; PostgreSQL health was instead directly demonstrated with pg_lsclusters and successful database queries.","The archive package installation reported that packages could not be authenticated, although apt policy showed they came from the configured official Ubuntu old-releases archive and post-install package health was clean."]}
